# Employment Management Portal — cron on managed/shared webspace
#
# This file replaces BOTH deploy/emp-scheduler.cron and deploy/emp-worker.service.
# Use it only where there is no root: IONOS webspace, cPanel and the like. On a
# server you own, use the other two — a daemon drains the queue in seconds where
# these entries take up to five minutes.
#
# On IONOS these are entered through Hosting → Cron Jobs in the panel rather than
# by copying this file anywhere. The schedules below are what to type in.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The two platform limits this works around
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   * A job may not repeat more often than every 5 minutes.
#   * Any run still going at 60 seconds is killed.
#
# The first is why the scheduler runs at */5 rather than the * * * * * that
# deploy/emp-scheduler.cron uses. It costs nothing here: every task in
# routes/console.php already falls on a 5-minute boundary —
#
#   attendance:remind-checkout   every 15 min   :00 :15 :30 :45
#   attendance:close-day         hourly         :00
#   reports:send                 hourly         :00
#   leave:process                daily          01:30
#   documents:check-expiry       daily          06:45
#   attendance:report-late       daily          10:30
#   db:backup --verify           daily          02:10
#
# — so a */5 cron fires schedule:run at every moment one of them is due. No
# schedule was changed to fit this host, and none should be: moving one off a
# 5-minute boundary would silently stop it running here.
#
# The second is why the queue entry carries --max-time=50. The worker exits
# cleanly at 50 seconds and the next run picks up where it left off; without it
# the platform kills mid-job at 60 and the job is left reserved until it times
# out.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set these two
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   APP  the absolute path to the directory containing artisan
#   PHP  the CLI binary, which is often NOT the same as the web PHP.
#        Find it with:  which php8.3  ||  ls /usr/bin/php*
#
APP=/homepages/nn/dnnnnnnnnn/htdocs/emp
PHP=/usr/bin/php8.3

MAILTO=ops@example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. The scheduler — every 5 minutes, on the boundary
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*/5 * * * * cd $APP && $PHP artisan schedule:run >> storage/logs/scheduler.log 2>&1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. The queue — offset by a minute so it never starts in the same second as
#    the scheduler and compete for the same 60-second budget.
#
#    --stop-when-empty  exit once drained rather than idling to the kill
#    --max-time=50      retire before the platform's 60-second cut
#    --tries/--backoff  match deploy/emp-worker.service, so a job behaves the
#                       same way on either host
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
1-56/5 * * * * cd $APP && $PHP artisan queue:work --stop-when-empty --max-time=50 --tries=3 --backoff=10,60,300 >> storage/logs/queue.log 2>&1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Also set, in .env:
#
#   HOSTING_MODE=managed
#
# Without it `emp:preflight` judges this install as though a daemon were running
# and fails the queue check the moment a job waits more than five minutes —
# which on a 5-minute cron is simply normal.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
